  "originalQuery": "A Database Engineer is working on a project that involves a multi-tenant SaaS application with a variety of workloads and access patterns. The application is currently using Cloud SQL for PostgreSQL, and the engineer is tasked with optimizing cost and performance. Which of the following strategies should the engineer implement to best achieve these objectives?",
  "originalOptions": "A. Implement a connection pooler to manage database connections efficiently<br/>B. Use Cloud Bigtable for its low-latency read and write capabilities<br/>C. Enable automatic storage increase to handle growing workloads<br/>D. Implement horizontal partitioning (sharding) to distribute data across multiple instances",
  "domain": "Deploy scalable and highly available databases in Google Cloud",
